The snippet shared Wednesday (Nov. 25), the late-night host and *NSYNC alum open with a spirited performance of DJ Casper&#8217;s &#8220;Cha Cha Slide,&#8221; complete, of course, with the song&#8217;s mandatory choreography. After hopping, two-stomping and sliding to the left and right, Fallon and Timberlake transition effortlessly into Earth, Wind & Fire&#8217;s &#8220;September,&#8221; with the pop star inviting the audience into the fun by getting up close to both secondary cameras on either side of the center lens.

Before the clip cuts off, the pair switches off again to another song, seamlessly jumping into the chorus of Kool & The Gang&#8217;s &#8220;Celebration.&#8221;

The full holiday episode will premiere at 11:35 p.m. on NBC. In addition to the full medley, fans can look forward to Timberlake performing at the Rainbow Room at Rockefeller Center, marking the first-ever Tonight Show broadcast from the venue.

Timberlake will certainly have plenty to discuss as well, as the singer is celebrating the 20th anniversary of his Billboard 200 -topping FutureSex/LoveSounds album. He also recently announced that he has a tell-all docuseries coming to Apple TV in December, touching on the highs and lows of his career, personal life and position in the public eye.

